b/sc8wdj.jpg"}, {"id": 415206, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc8wdi.jpg"}, {"id": 1618561, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scyow1.jpg"}, {"id": 1618559, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scyovz.jpg"}, {"id": 1618560, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scyow0.jpg"}], "slug": "harvest-moon-for-girl", "storyline": "The game starts with the player washed up and unconscious on the beach of Mineral Town. Suddenly, she has a flashback. In this flashback, she is on the side of a cruise ship staring at the sky and thinking about her life's direction. She then meets a poet and ends up spending a lot of time with him as he teaches her a lot about living.\n\nOne day, a storm hits the ship, causing a shipwreck. Claire then drifts onto the beach of Mineral Town, where she is rescued by Zack and a mystery boy. Claire then wakes up in an abandoned farm, and Mayor Thomas introduces himself to her. Because she has nowhere to go, Mayor Thomas allows Claire to live on the farm. Claire, who now has a bit of amnesia, remembers the words of the poet and finds a meaning in life. She then decides to raise the farm and hunts for the mystery boy.", "summary": "Harvest Moon for Girl is essentially Harvest Moon: Back to Nature with a slightly tweaked story, a few different gameplay mechanics, and the possibility to play as a girl.", "themes": [{"id": 28, "name": "Business"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/harvest-moon-for-girl", "videos": [{"id": 173072, "name": "Gameplay Video", "video_id": "hnQpuTXUzwE", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hnQpuTXUzwE", "title": "PlayStation - Bokujou Monogatari Harvest Moon for Girl (2000)", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/hnQpuTXUzwE/maxresdefault.jpg"}], "collections": [{"id": 596, "name": "Harvest Moon"}]}